\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Isothermal rate-integral speed estimates from \cref  {eq:speed-sensitivity}, relative to the exact phase-space estimate, at \(\mu _B=1200\,\mathrm  {MeV}\) and \(T=0,20,50,100\,\mathrm  {MeV}\). The four rate models use the same colors and line styles as the local-rate figures; blue and green labels give the Eq.~(23) and \((\mu _B/3)^5\) ratios at \(a(0^+)=1\). The exact phase-space and \(T^0+T^2\) curves coincide in the cold panel, which is explicitly a limiting rate-integral ratio. Only the reaction rate changes between models; these are sensitivity estimates, not numerically solved front velocities.}}{17}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
